    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener>
                    <dateline><date when="1947-05-09">May 9, 1947</date></dateline><salute>Dear <rs
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__4958" type="person">Dean Weigle</rs>:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>I have known <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4959" type="person">Mr. Charles Libby
                        Ives</rs> for the time he was studying in Union Theological Seminary. He is
                    a very attractive and genial young man who was eagerly interested in theological
                    and philosophical problems. He belonged to a group of students who dealt with
                    difficult questions of the relationship between physics and religion.</p>
                <p>His B. D. thesis dealing with the theology of <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1382"
                        type="person">Nestorius</rs> received an A-. Unfortunately I do not know
                    much about the work he has done since his graduation from Union Theological
                    Seminary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>Very sincerely yours,</salute>
                    <signed>
                        <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Prof. Paul
                        Tillich</rs></signed>
                </closer>

            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
